From: Percival Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: mask the ML peer id before clearing it on SSR

ath12k_mac_dp_peer_cleanup() releases the host-allocated ML peer id of
every MLO peer that was still present when firmware went down:

	rcu_assign_pointer(dp_hw->dp_peers[dp_peer->peer_id], NULL);
	clear_bit(dp_peer->peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);

dp_peer->peer_id is the composite id, not the bare one.  The station
setup path stores it unmasked:

	dp_params.peer_id = ahsta->ml_peer_id | ATH12K_PEER_ML_ID_VALID;

so the value carries ATH12K_PEER_ML_ID_VALID (BIT(13), i.e. +8192).
That is correct for the dp_peers[] lookup, which is sized
MAX_DP_PEER_LIST_SIZE (16384) precisely to be indexed by composite ids,
but it is wrong for free_ml_peer_id_map, which only has
ATH12K_MAX_MLO_PEERS bits.

The clear_bit() therefore addresses a bit roughly a kilobyte past the
end of the bitmap.  In struct ath12k_hw the bitmap is followed by the
embedded struct ath12k_dp_hw, whose first member is the dp_peers[] RCU
pointer array, so the write silently flips a bit inside a live
ath12k_dp_peer pointer.  The intended bit is never cleared either, so
every MLO station present at the crash leaks its ML peer id for good.

The path runs on every firmware recovery that had MLO peers associated,
which on IPQ5332 + QCN9274 access points is the common q6wcss fatal
error / PCIe RDDM case under load.

Mask the id back to the host domain before touching the bitmap, and
bound it defensively so a malformed id can never escape the map again.

Signed-off-by: Percival Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -1284,8 +1284,12 @@ void ath12k_mac_dp_peer_cleanup(struct a
 	spin_lock_bh(&dp_hw->peer_lock);
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(dp_peer, tmp, &dp_hw->dp_peers_list, list) {
 		if (dp_peer->is_mlo) {
+			u16 ml_peer_id = dp_peer->peer_id &
+					 ~ATH12K_PEER_ML_ID_VALID;
+
 			rcu_assign_pointer(dp_hw->dp_peers[dp_peer->peer_id], NULL);
-			clear_bit(dp_peer->peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
+			if (!WARN_ON_ONCE(ml_peer_id >= ATH12K_MAX_MLO_PEERS))
+				clear_bit(ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
 		}

 		list_move(&dp_peer->list, &peers);
